  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Jeep safaris in Pakistan</h2>
  <p>Many of the most beautiful places in Gilgit-Baltistan are reached by jeep tracks rather than roads. Our jeep safaris use local 4x4s and drivers who know these tracks, with hotels each night, and run on private dates.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/jeep-safaris/deosai-jeep-safari/">Deosai jeep safari</a> crosses the Deosai plateau, at about 4,000 metres, in five days from Skardu. The <a href="/jeep-safaris/shigar-basho-khaplu-jeep-safari/">Shigar, Basho and Khaplu jeep safari</a> takes six days through the valleys east of Skardu. The <a href="/jeep-safaris/mountains-villages-safari/">Mountains and Villages Jeep Safari</a> is a 22-day journey across the Northern Areas.</p>
  <p>Deosai is open only in summer, when the snow has cleared from the plateau road; we run it when the road is officially open. See our <a href="/destinations/deosai/">Deosai National Park guide</a> for the season.</p>
